# Dialogue and narration
@scenario tutorial_lesson_20
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide shy]
ginger: So far you've read my lines one at a time. Let's put the next one on a page and see how it feels.
[mode dialogue nvl]
narrator: This line is narration. It appears in the NVL layout.
[mode dialogue standard]
ginger: This line uses standard dialogue again. Find both mode commands in the script.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: Why restore the dialogue mode at the boundary?
> So the character art is deleted. -> retry
> So the next scene opens with its intended layout. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Presentation can persist across scene boundaries. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Presentation can persist across scene boundaries.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_20]
[flag tutorial_done_20]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_4]
